On the other hand, by exhaustive search we have checked that none of them has vertex set $D$. Thus $C_3\cup C_4$ is $\Z_{15}$-graceful but not $D$-graceful.

Here is instead an example of a $D$-admissible graph which is also $D$-graceful.
Let $D=\{1,4,5,6,7,9,11,16,17\}$ be the Paley $(19,9,4)$ difference set and let $\Gamma$ be the 3-prism.
A graceful Paley-labeling of $\Gamma$ is the following: 

